	// GetKeysEventPreferences Which of Keys' own events notify you
	//
	// EVERY CATEGORY KEYS POSTS UNDER, each with your three switches — in the app, by email, by
	// push — and what the company set for it: `none`, `default` (a starting point you may change)
	// or `required`.
	//
	// NOT GATED. It answers for the caller alone, in the account environment the credential acts
	// in. What you chose in another account environment is answered there.
	//
	// ONLY A PERSON HAS EVENT CHOICES. An agent or a machine is refused with 403
	// `ring_requires_person`.
	//
	// FIFTEEN CATEGORIES, one per event the Notification preferences page lists, each named by Keys
	// and permanent. Two are a steward's, one a check-out holder's, one a trusted person's (the spec
	// lane's rulings, 26 October 2026), one an asker's (ONPLO-3775) and the last a key's owners' (ONPLO-3199):
	//   `keys.key-found-in-breach`         a key of yours turning up in a known breach
	//   `keys.key-expiring`                a key expiring
	//   `keys.rotation-overdue`            a key's rotation falling overdue
	//   `keys.use-request-waiting`         a use request or a check-out waiting on you
	//   `keys.emergency-countdown-running` an emergency-access countdown running against you
	//   `keys.share-ending`                a share of yours ending
	//   `keys.hand-over-asked`             a hand-over ask after someone leaves
	//   `keys.company-key-rule-changed`    a company key rule that changed what you may do
	//   `keys.health-digest-ready`         the weekly health digest
	//   `keys.key-suspended`               a key you steward was suspended
	//   `keys.check-out-returned`          a privileged key you steward came back from a check-out
	//   `keys.check-out-ended`             a check-out of yours ended, forced back or timed out
	//   `keys.emergency-access-answered`   your ask for emergency access answered: shared, denied or removed
	//   `keys.ask-answered`                your ask to use or share a key answered
	//   `keys.legal-hold-ended`            a legal hold on a key you own or steward ended
	//
	// A CATEGORY YOU NEVER CHOSE answers where Keys starts it. The example shows the shape and
	// every category; it is not a promise of where each one starts.
	//
	// ACCOUNT'S GENERAL CHANNELS STILL DECIDE. A category with `email` on sends no email while
	// email is off in Account's Notification preferences. The choice here is kept and counts
	// again when the channel is back on.
	//
	// WHEN THE NOTIFICATIONS SERVICE CANNOT BE ASKED the answer is 503
	// `notifications_unavailable`, never the choices from a copy and never where each category
	// starts. The same request can be sent again.
