	// WHY, IN ONE LINE, AND FOR HOW LONG. The approver reads who is asking, which key, why and
	// for how long. The company key rules say both, once for every key in Check-out here: an ask
	// with no reason is refused with 422 `check_out_reason_required` while
	// `check_out_reason_required` is true, as it is where nobody set it, and a time longer than
	// `check_out_maximum_minutes` is refused `check_out_too_long` — four hours where nobody set
	// another. Where the rules ask for no reason, one given is still kept. THE RULES AS THEY
	// STAND AT THE ASK are what it is held to: an ask already made, or a key already held, is
	// never shortened or refused by a later change to them.
	//
	// THE OBJECT IS THE KEY. A check-out sits inside its key, so the permission is asked of the
	// key in the path, as revealing its value is.
