	// the key (decision 0707). Attachments keep working — a write-only entry is the only kind that
	// may be attached at all. (Until 5 November 2026 this said the previous values were destroyed
	// in the act, ONPLO-1530.)
	//
	// THE WAY BACK IS A NEW KEY. If the value has to be readable again, make a new readable entry,
	// type the value into it and move what uses the old one across. That is a new promise on a
	// new entry, never one withdrawn on an old one.
	//
	// ITS OWN OPERATION AND NOT A FIELD OF `updateKey` (decision 0547: an object's own rule gets
	// its own operation). `updateKey` is written in two places and is safe only because repeating
	// it converges; a turn that cannot be undone must not be able to land while a rename beside it
	// failed. Sending it for a key that is already write-only changes nothing and answers 200.
