// ListAttachments Where keys are used
//
// ONE RELATION, TWO VIEWS. Name a `key_id` and it answers where that key runs; name a target —
// `target_kind` and `target_id` together — and it answers what that flow project or deploy
// environment has been given. This is the audit answer to "which flow project holds which
// secret", and the thing to read before rotating or deleting.
//
// ONE VIEW A REQUEST, ALWAYS: a key, or a target, and never both or neither — the 422 at
// `/query` (`attachment_view_malformed`). The specification draws "One page, two views", and
// the vault, which holds the attachment (decision 0641), lists one side at a time. Until
// 2026-10-08 this said that naming neither answered every attachment of every key you may see,
// and that a `target_kind` alone narrowed it; neither was ever served.
//
// GATED BY SEEING THE KEY. An attachment of a key you may not see is absent — a whole view of a
// key you may not see is an empty page, never told apart from a key with no attachment.
//
// IN THE ORDER THEY WERE MADE, the vault's own.
//
// A CONNECTION IS NOT IN THIS LIST. A connection's credential is one record, the connection's
// own `credential_key_id`, and it is read from the Integrations API by that id — a second
// record here would be a copy that drifts.
//
// Corresponds with GET /attachments (the `ListAttachments` operationId).
