// AnswerGuestShareAskWithBody Approve or refuse somebody's share with an outside person
//
// APPROVE, OR REFUSE WITH A REASON (decision 0776, point 3). "Approve makes the share and
// tells both. Refuse with a reason makes nothing and tells the asker why." Approved, the ask is
// `approved` and the share is made as the asker asked for it: the same person, role and end,
// given by the asker. Refused, it is `refused` and nothing is given.
//
// NEVER YOUR OWN — `guest_share_own_ask`. "An approver can never sign their own ask," and
// holding the permission does not change it.
//
// THE RULES AS THEY STAND AT THE SIGNATURE. Approve asks again what the share asked: a key
// now in the Trash is `key_in_trash`, and one that may no longer go to an outside person, or
// a key group holding such a key, is `guest_sharing_not_allowed`. The ask stays `waiting`, so
// Refuse can still close it with a reason. Refuse is never refused for these.
//
// AN ASK NOBODY ANSWERED ENDS by itself when its "Access until" passes, "because there is
// nothing left to give" — `ended`. Answering one is `guest_share_ask_ended`.
//
// ANSWERED ONCE — `guest_share_ask_already_answered`. The same answer sent again by the same
// person changes nothing and answers the ask as it stands; another answer is refused.
//
// AN ASK WITHDRAWN BECAUSE ITS ASKER LEFT is answered as it stands, `withdrawn`, and nothing
// is written: "Nobody is left to use an approval, so nobody is asked to give one", and the
// approver sees why. Never your own still holds.
//
// ONE APPROVAL AT A TIME — `guest_share_ask_being_signed`. Approve asks identity to place the
// share between reading the ask and answering it, and any other answer in that moment is
// refused. Send it again a moment later and it meets the ask as it then stands.
//
// IDENTITY PLACES THE SHARE, GIVEN BY THE ASKER, as the approver signed it (decision 0958). Where
// it cannot, nothing is answered and the ask waits, so Refuse can still close it: nobody by the
// id the ask names is `recipient_not_found`; the person who asked may no longer give it, having
// left or lost the share themselves, is `guest_share_asker_no_longer_holds`; the end passed
// before the signature is `guest_share_ask_ended`; and identity that could not be asked is the
// 503, which means send the same answer again.
//
// THE KEY OR THE KEY GROUP MAY BE GONE SINCE THE ASK: `not_found` for a key, `key_ring_not_found` for
// a key group, as sharing it answers.
//
// WHO IS TOLD IS THE SPEC LANE'S RULING OF 29 OCTOBER 2026 (ONPLO-3775). The approver, while
// it waits, under `keys.use-request-waiting`, whose words stay "a use request or a check-out
// waiting on you": the Notification preferences page says in a sentence of its own that such
// a share waits under the same event. The asker, of Approve, Refuse with the reason, or the ask ending with
// nobody answering, under `keys.ask-answered`. The outside person only once the
// share is made: an Onplo person under a new category for a key or a key group shared with you, an
// email address by Account's guest invitation. That category is not in Keys' list yet: it
// arrives with the change that tells (ONPLO-1652).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with PUT /guest-share-asks/{guest_share_ask_id}/answer (the `AnswerGuestShareAsk` operationId).
