// ListHandOvers The leavers' hand-overs still open in this company
//
// WHEN A MEMBER LEAVES, THEIR READABLE KEYS ARE HANDED OVER. "Readable entries in their
// personal corner go to ... an Administrator, as a hand-over ask flagged 'Known by a leaver —
// rotate'." One ask per leaver (the spec lane's ruling, 26 October 2026): a personal corner has
// no steward, so the ask is the company's Administrators', and any one of them answers it.
//
// OPEN UNTIL EVERY KEY IN IT IS ANSWERED, or its window ends: Key rules → When a member leaves,
// 30 days. Then a key still unanswered goes to the Trash, never deleted for ever — unless a
// flow or a connection still uses it, which stays where it is, `still_used`, and Key health
// keeps listing it under 'Known by a leaver'.
//
// WRITE-ONLY KEYS ARE NEVER HERE: they are deleted the moment the member leaves, attached or not.
//
// NEWEST FIRST, by when the member left. A PAGE SERVED IS ONE LOOK, and it names no key.
