// key's value is still one call to the vault, and one line in the audit log.
//
// A SIGNATURE, WHERE THE KEY RULES ASK FOR ONE. Name the approved ask in `key_export_ask_id`. It
// covers exactly its keys, for one run, and only for the person who asked. The run spends it before
// the first value is read, so a run that fails halfway needs a new ask.
//
// A PRIVILEGED KEY GOES IN ONLY WITH AN APPROVED ASK OR AN OPEN CHECK-OUT OF YOURS when the export
// runs. Otherwise it is left out and named in the answer, and the rest still runs.
//
// A REVEAL FREEZE STOPS AN EXPORT — `reveal_frozen` — and `detail` carries the freeze's own reason.
// Nothing arms a freeze yet (ONPLO-3883), so nothing answers this today.
//
// THIS CALL ANSWERS WHAT ONE PERMISSION CHECK COVERS, 200 keys today. That is the size of one
// check and not the export's limit: a whole corner can leave as one file. As CSV, that is
// `exportKeyCornerAsCsv`, streamed to the download. As an archive it runs as a job, which is
// not declared yet (ONPLO-5528).
