// UpdateKeyWithBody Change a key
//
// Every field is optional; an omitted field is untouched, and an explicit `null` clears a field
// that may be empty. THE VALUE IS NOT HERE, neither is the key group, and neither is the turn to
// write-only — each has its own rule and its own operation.
//
// EVERY FIELD HERE IS SAFE TO SEND AGAIN, AND THAT IS A RULE OF THIS OPERATION. A key's name
// and scope are held by the vault and its steward, site, dates and Privileged setting by Keys
// (decision 0641), so one change is written in two places and can stop half applied. It is
// correct because sending the same change again finishes it. A field that cannot be repeated
// or undone does not belong here, which is why turning a key write-only was moved out on
// 2026-10-02 (`makeKeyWriteOnly`).
//
// PRIVILEGED IS A FIELD HERE BECAUSE THE SPECIFICATION LISTS IT AS ONE OF THE ENTRY'S, and it
// is both repeatable and undone by sending another. TURNING IT `off` IS NOT DONE HERE: it is
// "a permission of its own", and `turnKeyPrivilegedOff` asks it. A change naming `off` for a
// key set to Ask before use or Check-out is refused with 422 `privileged_off_needs_its_own_permission`,
// and nothing changes; naming `off` for a key that is `off` already changes nothing. Until
// 25 October 2026 this field turned it off too, under this permission alone. ON A
// COMPANY KEY IT IS NEVER BELOW THE COMPANY'S FLOOR FOR ITS KIND (`AlwaysPrivileged`) OR FOR
// THE KEY GROUP IT IS IN (`AlwaysPrivilegedRings`), whichever is higher: a change naming less is
// refused with 422 `privileged_below_company_rule`, and nothing changes. A change that leaves
// it out is not judged against the floor. A MEMBER'S OWN KEY INSIDE A COMPANY is held to the
// floor for its kind while the company's rules apply to personal keys
// (`PersonalKeysInsideTheCompany`), and changing one is never refused because the company
// keeps no personal keys: a rule never rewrites a key, and the key is already there.
//
// SHARING TO GUESTS IS SET HERE, ON A COMPANY KEY (`GuestSharing`): it is one of the company
// key's fields, and both repeatable and undone by sending another. Named on a personal key, it
// is refused with 422 `guest_sharing_on_a_personal_key`, and nothing changes. Switched to
// `not-allowed` while an outside person holds the key's key group, it is refused with 409
// `ring_held_by_an_outside_person`, whose `detail` names the share to cut first, and nothing
// changes (decision 0776).
//
// THE USE WINDOW IS SET HERE (`UseWindowMinutes`), repeatable and undone by sending another.
// On a company key, named longer than the company's Maximum duration on Check-outs
// (`check_out_maximum_minutes`) as it stands now, it is refused with 422
// `use_window_above_maximum_duration`, and nothing changes. A personal key's has no Maximum
// duration above it, only the day (ONPLO-1587).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /keys/{key_id} (the `UpdateKey` operationId).
func (c *Client) UpdateKeyWithBody(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewUpdateKeyRequestWithBody(c.Server, keyId, contentType, body)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

