// AcceptUnrotatedReturnWithBody Accept the risk of a privileged key that came back and was not rotated
//
// THE STEWARD'S REMINDER'S CLOSE AND DON'T REMIND (ONPLO-4304). "Close and don't remind is
// accepting the risk, so it needs Accept the risk of a value still out and a written reason,
// and the person who held the key can never press it." The permission is the company's: the
// catalogue grants it at the environment alone, so nothing is asked of the key.
//
// ONLY A CHECK-OUT THAT CAME BACK NOT ROTATED — `check_out_not_back_unrotated`. That is
// `closed` with `rotated_on_return: false` ("returned, not rotated yet"), or
// `live-value-still-out`. One never approved, still held, or rotated when it came back has no
// risk to accept. AT LAUNCH NOTHING ROTATES BY ITSELF (the owner, 24 October 2026), so every
// check-out that came back is accepted this way. A check-out whose time ran out is accepted
// once the returner has written it back, within a minute of its end.
//
// NEVER THE PERSON WHO HELD IT — `check_out_own_risk`, "whoever holds Approve somebody
// else's ask" or not.
//
// WHAT IT WRITES. Who accepted it, when, and the reason, on the check-out
// (`risk_accepted_by`, `risk_accepted_at`, `risk_reason`). Its state is unchanged: the value
// is still out, and a check-out that reads rotated while the value is live is "the one lie
// this page may never tell".
//
// THE REMINDER STOPS. The steward's reminder this return posted under
// `keys.check-out-returned` is taken back, in the same act, from every stream it is in, as a
// rotation takes it back. A return that reminded nobody has nothing to take back.
//
// ACCEPTED ONCE. A check-out accepted already changes nothing, whoever sends it again and
// with whatever reason, and answers the check-out as it stands: a look.
//
// A ROTATION BY HAND AFTER THE RETURN is not looked for. The key's own History says when its
// value changed; accepting a risk the rotation already ended records only that somebody did.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/check-outs/{check_out_id}/risk-accepted (the `AcceptUnrotatedReturn` operationId).
func (c *Client) AcceptUnrotatedReturnWithBody(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, checkOutId CheckOutId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewAcceptUnrotatedReturnRequestWithBody(c.Server, keyId, checkOutId, contentType, body)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

