// AnswerUseAskWithBody Approve or refuse somebody's ask to use a key
//
// APPROVE, OR REFUSE WITH A REASON. "It is answered by whoever holds Approve somebody else's
// ask, or the approve-only right on that key or its key group, and never by the asker." Approved,
// "the asker may reveal and use the key" until `usable_until`. "Refuse with a reason lets
// nothing through." The approve-only right answers and never reveals: revealing asks its own
// permission.
//
// NEVER YOUR OWN — `use_ask_own_ask`. Holding either permission does not change it.
//
// ANSWERED ONCE — `use_ask_already_answered`. The same answer sent again by the same person
// changes nothing and answers the ask as it stands; another answer is refused.
//
// APPROVE CHECKS THE ASKER IS STILL HERE, as answering a check-out does. An approval of a
// leaver's ask answers 200 with the ask `withdrawn`, and nothing is let through. A refusal
// asks nothing about the asker. When identity cannot be asked who is a member, nothing is
// approved and the answer is 503, which means ask again.
//
// A WITHDRAWN ASK HAS NOTHING LEFT TO ANSWER. Any answer to one changes nothing and answers
// it as it stands.
//
// "EITHER ANSWER TELLS THE ASKER", once, under `keys.ask-answered`, for your information:
// approved with until when, or refused with the reason. A withdrawal tells nobody.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with PUT /keys/{key_id}/use-asks/{use_ask_id}/answer (the `AnswerUseAsk` operationId).
