	// A KEY IN THE TRASH IS LEFT OUT unless `in_trash` asks for the Trash instead.
	//
	// THE TRASH ENDS IN ITS GHOSTS (decision 0672). A key deleted for good while a legal hold
	// covers it leaves use at once and stays under the Trash filter, after the keys in the Trash,
	// carrying `kept_by_legal_hold`. Which are drawn, and for whom, is the deletion service's to
	// say (decision 0686): the person a hidden hold names sees no ghost, and is answered exactly
	// what a key simply gone would answer. When the deletion service cannot be asked, no ghost is
	// drawn and the rest of the Trash is listed.
	//
	// A LIST IS REFUSED RATHER THAN CUT SHORT — `reach_too_wide`. The list is drawn from where
	// your grants sit, and one list covers grants on at most 500 key groups and at most 500 single
	// keys. Somebody granted more than either is answered a 409 and no keys, because a list drawn
	// from the first 500 would have keys missing with nothing saying so. It is a limit of this
	// service and not a mistake in the request: no narrowing gets past it, and asking again
	// answers the same until the grants change — one grant on a key group in place of many on its
	// keys. A grant on the whole account environment is never refused this way.
