// never touches the value.
//
// BOTH ARE ASKED, IN ONE QUESTION (decision 0632, rule 6). The object is the KEY, so one half
// asks whether you may attach THIS key; the other asks whether you may give a key to THE
// TARGET — "You may only pick a target you hold the attach permission on" — with Flows' own
// permission for it (`flows:project-key.create`). A target that does not exist, or that you
// may not give to, is refused `permission_missing` alike, never told apart. (Until
// 2026-10-08 this asked about the key alone and declared `target_not_found`, which nothing
// can tell apart from a target you may not see; nothing was served.)
//
// A FLOW PROJECT ONLY, FOR NOW. A deploy environment does not exist until Flows registers
// them (ONPLO-1180), and its own permission, `flows:environment-key.create`, is chosen by the
// TARGET's kind — which no contract can say yet (ONPLO-1868). The request takes
// `flow-project` alone until both land; the answer, `Attachment`, keeps both kinds, because
// the vault may hold either.
//
// THE ATTACHMENT IS THE VAULT'S (decision 0641); its note is Keys'. A key in the Trash is
// refused `key_in_trash` — restore it first; an alias the target already uses for another key
// is refused `alias_taken`.
