// ListCheckOutAsksWithResponse The check-out asks you may answer
//
// THE PENDING ASKS: "a second list on the same page, longest waiting first: who is asking,
// which key, why in one line, and for how long — answered with Approve or Refuse with a reason"
// (`answerCheckOut`). Each is a check-out in the state `asked`. One that was answered leaves
// this list: approved, it is on `listCheckOuts`; refused, it is on neither.
//
// "THE PENDING ASKS SHOW ONLY TO WHOEVER MAY ANSWER THEM." See the check-out asks you may answer
// (`keys:check-out-ask.read`) is given to every role that holds Approve somebody else's ask, and
// to whoever holds Approve a reveal without ever seeing the value, so a trusted person can find
// the ask they may answer. It is offered in a personal environment and a business one, and it
// can be given on one key or its key group. An ask sits inside its key, so the door asks no
// permission, and each row is judged by its key. An ask you may not see is absent, never masked.
//
// YOUR OWN ARE ALWAYS HERE. "A person always sees their own asks and their own check-outs, with
// or without it": an ask you made is listed whatever you were given. It is shown and never
// yours to answer: approving your own is refused inside `answerCheckOut`.
//
// THE LONGEST WAITING FIRST, by when each was asked for. The page said "worst first" until 26
// October 2026, and this contract read it this way; the spec lane confirmed the reading and the
// page now says it.
//
// A GUEST SHARE THAT NEEDS A SIGNATURE waits under the same PENDING ASKS on the page, and is
// read with `listGuestShareAsks`: it is answered under a permission of its own, given across
// the account environment, where a check-out's is given on a key. The page shows both lists'
// rows in one, longest waiting first.
//
// A PAGE SERVED IS ONE LOOK, an empty one too, and it names no ask.
