//
// WHO HOLDS WHICH PRIVILEGED KEY, WHY AND UNTIL WHEN, and what happened when each came back.
// "One list, saved views — never tabs. The views are Open · History", so `view` says which,
// and a check-out moves from one to the other when it comes back.
//
// EACH CHECK-OUT IS ASKED ABOUT, BY ITS KEY, NEVER THE WHOLE ENVIRONMENT. See check-outs
// (`keys:check-out.read`) can be given on one key or its key group, and a check-out sits inside its
// key. So the door asks no permission, and each row is judged by its key: somebody given it on
// one key is answered that key's check-outs. A check-out you may not see is absent, never
// masked.
//
// YOUR OWN ARE ALWAYS HERE. "A person always sees their own asks and their own check-outs, with
// or without it": a check-out you hold, or held, is listed whatever you were given.
//
// ONLY CHECK-OUTS THAT RAN. An ask nobody has answered, and one that was refused, never held a
// key, and they are not on this list: "PENDING ASKS stays its own thing, because a request is a
// different object." The asks nobody has answered are `listCheckOutAsks`; a refused one is on
// neither list.
//
// OPEN is every check-out still out: held, coming back, or back with its value still live.
// HISTORY is every one that is over. A check-out whose time is up is over, and is in History
// before the returner has written it down.
//
// NEWEST FIRST, in both views, by when it was asked for. "The row stays at the top of Open until
// somebody rotates it by hand or accepts the risk" is not built: nothing tries a rotation yet,
// so no check-out is ever back with its value still live, and that order comes with the first
// rotation that can fail (ONPLO-1587). Accepting the risk is `acceptUnrotatedReturn`; until
// 8 November 2026 this said the order came with it.
//
// A PAGE SERVED IS ONE LOOK, an empty one too, and it names no check-out.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /check-outs (the `ListCheckOuts` operationId).
