// (decision 0663). In a personal one there are no company key rules to see, and the answer is
// a 404 with the code `environment_has_no_company_side`. Where the authorization service did
// not say which kind of account environment the request is in, it is
// `authorization_unavailable` — ask again — and never that 404: not known is not personal.
//
// A MEMBER NEEDS NO PERMISSION TO READ THE SENTENCE A RULE PUTS ON THEIR OWN KEY; that
// sentence travels with the key. This operation is the Key rules page.
//
// SEEING THE RULES IS RECORDED. Each look that is answered leaves one audit event — the rules
// its target, about nobody, marked a look and naming no change — as every look does, and not
// only a look at a secret (decision 0675). A look that was refused saw nothing and leaves none.
