// UpdateCompanyKeyRulesWithBodyWithResponse Set the company key rules
//
// EVERY FIELD IS OPTIONAL, AND AN OMITTED RULE IS UNTOUCHED. The answer is the whole set as
// it now stands. Sent again, the same change changes nothing.
//
// A RULE FLAGS AND BLOCKS A NEW SAVE; IT NEVER REWRITES OR DELETES A KEY. Lowering how many
// previous values are kept trims nothing by itself: a key's history is trimmed to the new
// number the next time that key's value is rotated.
//
// ONLY WHERE THERE IS A COMPANY SIDE, as `getCompanyKeyRules` says, with the same two answers.
//
// ALWAYS PRIVILEGED IS SENT WHOLE, the kinds and the key groups each: a list replaces the one that
// stood, and the same kind or key group named twice is refused (422 `company_key_rules_malformed`).
// A list that says what stands already, in any order, changes nothing. EACH KEY GROUP NAMED IS ONE
// OF THE COMPANY'S in this account environment, asked of the vault before anything changes:
// a key group that is not there, or one of somebody's own, is refused with 422
// `always_privileged_ring_not_found`, and which of the two it was is not said.
//
// KEY GROUPS SHAREABLE TO GUESTS IS SENT WHOLE in the same way, each key group with whether an approver
// signs: the same key group named twice is refused (422 `company_key_rules_malformed`), and a key group
// that is not one of the company's is refused with 422 `guest_shareable_ring_not_found`.
//
// PERSONAL KEYS INSIDE THE COMPANY IS SENT WHOLE, both of its halves. Turned off, it stops
// new personal keys and key groups of one's own in the company, and the ones already there stay
// as they are.
//
// THE CHECK-OUT SETTINGS — Maximum duration and Reason required — hold for every key in
// Check-out in this account environment, never per key. They are read when somebody asks for
// a check-out (`requestCheckOut`), and a change reaches the next ask only.
//
// A CHANGE IS RECORDED WITH THE NUMBER BEFORE AND AFTER, the always-privileged kinds and
// key groups before and after, each with its floor, personal keys inside the company before and
// after, each check-out setting before and after, and the key groups shareable to guests before
// and after, each with whether an approver signs. One audit event for a change that
// really moved a rule — the rules its target, about nobody, marked a change — saying what the
// rule stood at and what it stands at. A save that moved nothing names no change and still
// shows the rules, so it is recorded as a look (decision 0685).
//
// MORE THAN TEN PREVIOUS VALUES IS PREMIUM'S (decision 0822): "FREE KEEPS TEN, PREMIUM KEEPS
// UP TO 100". Raising the number above ten, and above what it stands at, needs Keys' Premium
// seat held by the one making the change. Without it the change is refused with 409
// `not_in_plan`, saying what is not included, and nothing changes. A RULE ALREADY SET STANDS
// IF THAT SEAT LAPSES: fifty stays fifty, and every rotation keeps fifty. LOWERING IT NEVER
// NEEDS A SEAT, and neither does the number already held sent again. Up to ten, Account is
// not asked at all; above it, Account out of reach is 503 `account_unavailable` only where
// the seat was needed.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /company-key-rules (the `UpdateCompanyKeyRules` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) UpdateCompanyKeyRulesWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*UpdateCompanyKeyRulesResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.UpdateCompanyKeyRulesWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseUpdateCompanyKeyRulesResponse(rsp)
}

