// CreateKeyRingWithBodyWithResponse Make a key group
//
// A named group of keys shared, governed and hidden as one container — the office key group, a
// client key group, a team's key group. KEY GROUPS ARE FLAT, and that is the security model: a nested
// container means a grant on the parent reaches the children, which is the inheritance this
// app removes everywhere else. So a key group names no parent, here or ever.
//
// IT POINTS AT NO OBJECT, AND THAT IS A STATEMENT. A key group sits inside nothing — Keys has no
// top level (decision 0522) — so there is no container for "may I make one here" to be about,
// and the question is asked of the whole environment (decision 0632). A root for key groups to sit
// under was refused on purpose: it is the one thing a grant could reach every key group through.
//
// A COMPANY KEY GROUP IS MADE ONLY WHERE THERE IS A COMPANY SIDE: a business account environment,
// or Onplo's own team (decision 0663). Asked for in a personal one, it is refused with a 422
// whose error points at `/body/owner_scope` with the code
// `company_ring_in_a_personal_environment`, and nothing is made. Where the authorization
// service did not say which kind of account environment the request is in, a company key group is
// answered `authorization_unavailable` — ask again — and never that refusal: not known is not
// personal. A key group of your own is made in any kind, EXCEPT IN A COMPANY THAT KEEPS NO
// PERSONAL KEYS (`PersonalKeysInsideTheCompany`): there a key group of your own would be a
// personal corner, and it is refused with a 422 whose error points at `/body/owner_scope`
// with the code `personal_ring_not_allowed`, and nothing is made.
