// ForceCheckOutReturnWithBodyWithResponse Take a privileged key back before its timer ends
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, "never a button everyone who can see the page holds". Forcing a key
// back "tells the holder, records the reason, and runs rotation on return exactly as if they
// had handed it back".
//
// ONLY A CHECK-OUT THAT IS HELD — `check_out_not_held`. One that was never approved, or has
// already come back, has nothing to take.
//
// WHAT COMES BACK. The check-out is `returning` while the key's value is replaced, then
// `closed`. When the replacement does not go through it is `live-value-still-out`, and it
// stays that until somebody rotates the key by hand: "A check-out that reads closed while the
// value is still live is the one lie this page may never tell."
//
// THE KEY'S STEWARD IS REMINDED TO CHANGE THE VALUE while the company's
// `check_out_rotate_on_return` is on, as it is where nobody set it: once, by the call that
// brought the key back, under `keys.check-out-returned`, "waiting on you". A person or a team,
// as the key names it. A key with no steward, or a steward who took it back themselves, is not told.
//
// THE REMINDER GOES AWAY BY ITSELF THE MOMENT THE KEY IS ROTATED (the Check-outs page):
// `rotateKeyValue` takes back every reminder a return of the key posted that is still out.
//
// THE HOLDER IS TOLD, once, by the same call, under `keys.check-out-ended`, "for your
// information": the key's name, that it was forced back, and who took it. The reason stays on
// the check-out, where the holder reads it, and is never posted. A holder who took it back
// themselves is not told what they just did.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/check-outs/{check_out_id}/forced-return (the `ForceCheckOutReturn` operationId).
