// RemindAboutReturnLaterWithResponse Put off the reminder to change a returned key's value, for a day
//
// THE STEWARD'S REMINDER'S REMIND ME LATER (ONPLO-4304). "Remind me later needs no
// permission: whoever the reminder reached may press it, because it accepts nothing. It asks
// again 24 hours later, and the History row keeps reading 'returned, not rotated yet'." So
// nothing is asked of identity.
//
// ONLY WHOEVER THE REMINDER REACHED — `check_out_reminder_not_yours`: the key's steward, as
// the key names them. A check-out you may not see, of a key you may not see, is answered as
// one that does not exist. A KEY WHOSE STEWARD IS A TEAM is refused for now —
// `check_out_reminder_to_a_team`: identity tells Keys nothing of who is in a team, so Keys
// cannot say whom the reminder reached (ONPLO-4304 carries it).
//
// ONLY A REMINDER THAT IS OUT — `check_out_no_reminder_out`. A return that reminded nobody,
// one whose key was rotated since, and one whose risk was accepted have none.
//
// WHAT IT DOES. The reminder is taken back, in this act, from every stream it is in, and
// `reminds_again_at` is 24 hours from now. Then Keys posts it again, to the steward the key
// names then. A rotation of the key, or Close and don't remind (`acceptUnrotatedReturn`),
// before that moment ends it for good.
//
// PUT OFF ONCE AT A TIME. A reminder put off already changes nothing, and answers the
// check-out as it stands: a look.
//
// IT ACCEPTS NOTHING. The check-out's state, `rotated_on_return` and its acceptance are
// unchanged.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/check-outs/{check_out_id}/reminder-later (the `RemindAboutReturnLater` operationId).
