// it came back: handed back before, taken back, or its time up.
//
// WHAT COMES BACK. "Return or timeout closes the check-out." With Rotate on return switched
// on, the key's value is replaced where the system supports rotation. AT LAUNCH NOTHING
// ROTATES BY ITSELF (the owner, 24 October 2026): the check-out is `closed` with
// `rotated_on_return: false`, and its History row reads "returned, not rotated yet".
//
// THE KEY'S STEWARD IS REMINDED TO CHANGE THE VALUE while the company's
// `check_out_rotate_on_return` is on, as it is where nobody set it: once, by the call that
// brought the key back, under `keys.check-out-returned`, "waiting on you". A person or a team,
// as the key names it. A key with no steward, or a steward who handed it back themselves, is not told.
//
// THE REMINDER GOES AWAY BY ITSELF THE MOMENT THE KEY IS ROTATED (the Check-outs page):
// `rotateKeyValue` takes back every reminder a return of the key posted that is still out.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/check-outs/{check_out_id}/return (the `ReturnCheckOut` operationId).
