// DeleteKeyForEverWithResponse Delete a key in the Trash for ever
//
// "DELETE FOR EVER ERASES IT NOW AND ASKS ONCE, AND IT IS NEVER AN AI AGENT'S TO PRESS." The
// key leaves use at once and cannot come back: from this answer on, every operation here
// answers it as an id that names nothing. Its value is erased when the deletion service asks
// the vault for it, which is not while a legal hold covers it.
//
// UNDER A LEGAL HOLD IT IS NEVER REFUSED (decision 0672). A held key deleted for ever leaves
// use at once and "stays under the Trash filter as a ghost: greyed, 'Kept by a legal hold'" —
// shown by the list of the Trash, not by this answer (ONPLO-1527).
//
// ONLY A KEY IN THE TRASH — `key_not_in_trash`. Trash is the only way out, so a key in use is
// moved to the Trash first and is never erased in one step.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION (decision 0651), never the one that put it in the Trash.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/delete-for-ever (the `DeleteKeyForEver` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) DeleteKeyForEverWithResponse(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*DeleteKeyForEverResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.DeleteKeyForEver(ctx, keyId, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseDeleteKeyForEverResponse(rsp)
}

// FillKeyValueWithBodyWithResponse Hand a readable key's value to a login field on your own device
//
// AUTOFILL: USE A KEY WITHOUT READING IT (decision 0524). The browser extension or the phone's
// credential provider puts the value into a login field you tapped, and nobody is shown it. A
// fill is a USE and never a look, so it is gated by `keys:key-use.run` and not by
// `keys:key-value.read`, and it is never recorded as a reveal (decision 0983).
//
// ONE LINE PER FILL, AND IT IS THE VAULT'S: a use of the key, naming the site it was filled on,
// written before the value is answered. A retry is a second fill with its own line. What Keys
// refuses at its own door is one refused change, the key its target.
//
// YOU, FILLING FOR YOURSELF, AND NOBODY ELSE YET. A fill an AI agent asks for — one passkey
// touch by a person per use, naming the entry, the site and the agent — is not served yet: its
// line needs who approved it and when the approval ran out, which the audit envelope cannot
// say yet (ONPLO-4734). Until then an agent meets `passkey_proof_required`, final for it, as on
// a reveal.
//
// THE ADDRESS IS ONE OF THE KEY'S OWN, or nothing is handed over — `fill_site_not_the_keys`.
// `origin` is compared with the origin of the key's `site` and with each of its
// `also_fills_on`; a key with neither fills nowhere. Asking a person before filling on an
// address the key does not hold, and adding it on a yes, wait on two rulings (ONPLO-5293):
// until then that fill is refused, and the address is added on the key with `updateKey`.
//
// IT ASKS YOU TO PROVE IT IS YOU AGAIN, as a reveal does and on the same window: "a passkey
// touch before a readable secret half is shown, copied or filled". Refused
// `passkey_proof_required` until you do, cleared by `startPasskeyProof` and
// `completePasskeyProof` on the identity API.
//
// REFUSED BY WHAT THE KEY IS: a write-only key is never filled into a page, by anybody
// (`key_write_only`); a key in the Trash is restored first (`key_in_trash`); a suspended key is
// refused, "autofill refuses it" (`key_suspended`); a privileged key fills only inside what was
// approved (`key_use_not_approved`, `key_not_checked_out_to_you`), as a reveal does.
//
// A DEVICE DEVICES SAID WAS WIPED IS REFUSED — `device_wiped` — before anything else.
//
// A REVEAL FREEZE DOES NOT STOP IT. A freeze masks values and "never stops a USE".
//
// YOUR OWN AUTOFILL SETTINGS ARE HELD (ONPLO-4896): a site you said never to fill is refused
// (`fill_site_never_filled`), and so is a key in a key group you left out of the key groups autofill may
// use (`fill_ring_not_for_autofill`). Both are judged before the key's own site. They are set
// with `setKeysAutofillSettings`.
//
// YOUR COMPANY'S "AUTOFILL ONLY ON MANAGED DEVICES" IS HELD (ONPLO-4897): when its Key rules
// turn it on, Devices is asked whether this session's device is managed and compliant, and a
// device that is not, or a session that names no device, is refused (`fill_device_not_managed`).
// When Devices cannot be asked, nothing is filled (`devices_unavailable`), never filled on a
// guess. The rule is `autofill_only_on_managed_devices` on `updateCompanyKeyRules`.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES NOT HOLD YET, said rather than discovered: whether cards and identity
// documents are offered waits on a fill of a card.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/fill (the `FillKeyValue` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) FillKeyValueWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*FillKeyValueResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.FillKeyValueWithBody(ctx, keyId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseFillKeyValueResponse(rsp)
}

