// turn it on, Devices is asked whether this session's device is managed and compliant, and a
// device that is not, or a session that names no device, is refused (`fill_device_not_managed`).
// When Devices cannot be asked, nothing is filled (`devices_unavailable`), never filled on a
// guess. The rule is `autofill_only_on_managed_devices` on `updateCompanyKeyRules`.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES NOT HOLD YET, said rather than discovered: whether cards and identity
// documents are offered waits on a fill of a card.
//
// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/fill (the `FillKeyValue` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) FillKeyValueWithResponse(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, body FillKeyValueJSONRequestBody, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*FillKeyValueResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.FillKeyValue(ctx, keyId, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseFillKeyValueResponse(rsp)
}

// ShareKeyWithBodyWithResponse Share a key
//
// "Share a key or a whole key group with a member, a team or an outside person through the one
// share panel — roles Viewer · Editor · Manager." This shares ONE KEY. A share on its key group
// reaches it as well, and one placed here "can only add to it".
//
// ONE OF THREE ROLES, each the register's `keys.role.<this word>`, the three the catalogue's
// share action offers. "Approve only, never reads" is not one of them: it is "a right of its own
// and not a fourth share role", and which act gives it is not ruled yet.
//
// WITH A MEMBER OR A TEAM OF THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT. Nobody by that id here, or no such team,
// is refused (409 `recipient_not_found`), AND SO IS AN ONPLO PERSON WHO IS NOT A MEMBER HERE:
// sharing with an outside person is `shareKeyOutward`, which asks Account's permission as well
// (decision 0658). That refusal asks the identity service who is a member, and the server hands
// Keys that client in the change after the one that wrote this sentence (ONPLO-1652); until
// then it is not asked, and nothing reaches outside by it, because the identity service places
// a grant on no person yet (ONPLO-2884). A PERSONAL ENVIRONMENT HAS NO MEMBER BUT ITS OWN
// PERSON, so from there every share with somebody else is that operation's.
//
// A KEY IN THE TRASH CANNOT BE SHARED, "and that is the only kind that cannot" (409
// `key_in_trash`): restore it first. A write-only key is shared like any other and still shows
// its value to nobody. A privileged key is shared like any other and every use still asks.
//
// SHARING AGAIN CHANGES THE SHARE THAT IS THERE. A holder has one grant per object (decision
// 0650), so a person or a team shared with again takes the new role and the new end and keeps
// the id. `created` says which it was and the status is `200` either way: a retry after a
// timeout reads `false` and the same share, never a second one.
//
// `access_until` IS THE MOMENT THIS SHARE ENDS, and the time zone it was chosen in (decision
// 0650). Left out, the share has no end. A moment that has already passed is refused (422
// naming `access_until`, `access_until_passed`). "'Access until' on a guest grant" is required,
// and `shareKeyOutward` holds it.
//
// WHO MAY SHARE IT: whoever holds `keys:key.share` on the key or on its key group. "A Manager may
// share on what was shared with them; a Viewer or Editor may not."
//
// NOBODY IS TOLD BY THIS CALL. Keys' fifteen event categories name a share ending and none a
// share made, so there is nothing to post under.
//
// NEVER AN AI AGENT'S TO DO, and never a raw key's: a share is a grant of access (403
// `ring_requires_person`).
//
// THE IDENTITY SERVICE KEEPS THE GRANT, AND WRITES IT ITSELF. When it cannot be reached, 503
// `identity_unavailable`: whether the share landed is not known, so send the same request
// again. It is the same act, and answers the share that is there.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /keys/{key_id}/grants (the `ShareKey` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ShareKeyWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ShareKeyResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ShareKeyWithBody(ctx, keyId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseShareKeyResponse(rsp)
}

