// RotateKeyValueWithBodyWithResponse Rotate a key's value
//
// Its own operation because it has its own rule (decision 0547): the new value is typed ONCE,
// and everything attached picks it up BY NAME on its next run, with no redeploy. A field in a
// patch body cannot carry that, and a value must never ride beside a rename.
//
// WHAT HAPPENS TO THE OLD VALUE DEPENDS ON THE READABILITY. On a readable entry it moves to
// the previous values. On a write-only one it is out of use at once and all anybody can learn
// of it is when it changed and by whom. It is set aside, returned by no call, until the
// deletion service asks for it to be erased: at its next turn, or at its first turn after the
// release of a legal hold that covers the key (decision 0707). (Until 5 November 2026 this said
// nothing was kept, ONPLO-1530.)
//
// HOW MANY PREVIOUS VALUES A READABLE KEY KEEPS. A company key keeps what the company key
// rules say. A key of somebody's own follows its owner's Keys Premium seat, whoever rotates
// it: a hundred while the owner holds it, and otherwise ten or the number it already keeps,
// whichever is larger — ending Premium never shrinks what a key keeps (decision 0824). The
// oldest beyond that number leave use in this rotation and are set aside the same way.
//
// THE STEWARD'S REMINDER TO CHANGE THE VALUE GOES AWAY (ONPLO-1587). A privileged key that came
// back from a check-out reminded its steward under `keys.check-out-returned`, and "the reminder
// goes away by itself the moment the key is rotated" (the Check-outs page). So this rotation
// takes back every such reminder of the key that is still out, in the same act, from every
// stream it is in. A rotation sent twice takes back nothing the second time.
//
// THE ANSWER CARRIES NO VALUE, the one just sent included.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /keys/{key_id}/value (the `RotateKeyValue` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) RotateKeyValueWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, keyId KeyId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*RotateKeyValueResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.RotateKeyValueWithBody(ctx, keyId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseRotateKeyValueResponse(rsp)
}

