// RequestEmergencyAccessWithResponse Ask for access to the keys of somebody who named you
//
// PRESSED WHERE THE ROW IS SEEN. "Somebody who is not a member of the company asks from their
// Personal environment and never enters the company to ask." So a row is asked from wherever
// `listPeopleWhoNamedMe` shows it, and a row it does not show answers as one that names
// nothing.
//
// NO PERMISSION. "Asking needs no permission ... Being named is what lets a person ask, and no
// role can give or withhold it."
//
// IT STARTS THE COUNTDOWN AND GIVES NOTHING YET. The row becomes `requested`, with the moment
// you asked and the moment the waiting period runs out. "Asking makes them nothing there: the
// request and its countdown show on your row and in your security alerts, and nowhere else in
// the company, until a share is made."
